---
description: lean tools - batch reads and edits, compact command output
alwaysApply: true
---

The lean MCP server adds tools that save turns and tokens:

- MultiRead: read several files, or line ranges of them, in one call instead of one read per file.
- BatchEdit: when a change needs more than one edit, make all of them in a single call. No prior read needed; copy the old text from grep output.
- RunCompact: run tests, builds and linters through it when the output is long; it returns the exit status, error lines with context and the tail.

If a `lean-repo-map` rule is present, use its file and symbol list to go straight to the right file and line range instead of exploring with ls, find or broad greps.
